qant-native-computing-toolkit (2.5.0-0) stable; urgency=low

  * DFT support: new dft() for batched complex-to-complex DFTs on
    bcomplex32 (kDLBcomplex) tensors.
  * DLPack updated to v1.4.
  * npu_id is now a signed 32-bit integer everywhere;
    QANT_NATIVE_COMPUTING_TOOLKIT_AUTO_NPU_ID (-1) selects the first NPU that
    supports the requested operation. Values below -1 are rejected with an
    error.
  * get_sensor_info() and get_version_info() now return an error
    code and write their result into an out-parameter, instead of returning
    a zeroed struct on failure.
  * init_npu(), release_npu(), get_driver_info(), reset_perf_counter() and
    get_perf_counter() now follow the common error convention: 0 on
    success, -1 on failure with the error message printed to stderr.
  * New get_capabilities() reports which operations an NPU supports, as a
    list of QantDeviceCapability (Mul, NonLin, Dft, MemHandling).
  * get_available_npus() takes a list of QantDeviceCapability (Mul, NonLin,
    Dft, MemHandling) and lists only the NPUs that support all of them,
    sorted by id. An empty list returns all NPUs.
  * get_available_npus() and QANT_NATIVE_COMPUTING_TOOLKIT_DEFAULT_CHAR_ARR_LENGTH
    moved to qant_native_computing_toolkit_generic.h.

 -- Q.ANT GmbH <info@qant.de>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

